%% generated by make_ol.py from src/T7.txt; edit the source, not this file

1. The UN Declaration on the Elimination of Violence against Women (DEVAW) was adopted on:
(A) 18 December 1979  (B) 20 December 1993  (C) 4 September 1995  (D) 25 November 1999
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 20 December 1993^^ — 20 December 1993.

2. DEVAW Article 2 names three sites of violence. Which is NOT one of them?
(A) The family  (B) The community  (C) The State  (D) The market
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) The market^^ — The family, the community and the State.

3. CEDAW General Recommendation 19 (1992) declared gender-based violence a form of:
(A) Discrimination  (B) Crime  (C) Torture  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Discrimination^^ — Discrimination; updated by GR 35 (2017).

4. In the Beijing Platform, violence against women is Critical Area:
(A) A  (B) B  (C) G  (D) D
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) D^^ — Critical Area D.

5. The International Day for the Elimination of Violence against Women is:
(A) 8 March  (B) 25 November  (C) 10 December  (D) 12 February
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 25 November^^ — 25 November, start of the 16 Days of Activism ending on 10 December.

6. The Istanbul Convention on violence against women was adopted by the Council of Europe in:
(A) 1993  (B) 2006  (C) 2011  (D) 2017
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 2011^^ — 2011.

7. SDG target 5.3 calls for eliminating:
(A) Child, early and forced marriage  (B) All violence against women  (C) Unpaid care work  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Child, early and forced marriage^^ — Child, early and forced marriage (5.2 is all violence).

8. About how many women and girls were killed by partners or family members in 2023 (UNODC and UN Women)?
(A) 5,100  (B) 21,000  (C) 51,100  (D) 85,000
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 51,100^^ — About 51,100 — one every 10 minutes (85,000 killed intentionally in all).

9. Violence against women as a "continuum" (1988) was described by:
(A) Lori Heise  (B) Lenore Walker  (C) Evan Stark  (D) Liz Kelly
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Liz Kelly^^ — Liz Kelly.

10. Bandura's Bobo doll experiments (1961) showed that children:
(A) Copy aggression they observe  (B) Are born aggressive  (C) Never copy adults  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Copy aggression they observe^^ — Children imitate observed aggression.

11. The resource theory of family violence (1971) was proposed by:
(A) Johan Galtung  (B) Murray Straus  (C) Albert Bandura  (D) William Goode
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) William Goode^^ — William Goode.

12. *Violence Against Wives* (1979) was written by:
(A) Dobash and Dobash  (B) Pence and Paymar  (C) Thaddeus and Maine  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Dobash and Dobash^^ — R. Emerson Dobash and Russell Dobash.

13. *Against Our Will* (1975), arguing that rape is about power, was written by:
(A) Andrea Dworkin  (B) Kate Millett  (C) Catharine MacKinnon  (D) Susan Brownmiller
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Susan Brownmiller^^ — Susan Brownmiller.

14. The "cycle of violence" and "learned helplessness" were described in *The Battered Woman* (1979) by:
(A) Lenore Walker  (B) Liz Kelly  (C) Ellen Pence  (D) Evan Stark
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Lenore Walker^^ — Lenore Walker.

15. The Power and Control Wheel was developed in:
(A) Toronto  (B) Islamabad  (C) Chiswick, London  (D) Duluth, Minnesota
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Duluth, Minnesota^^ — Duluth, by the Domestic Abuse Intervention Project (from 1981).

16. *Coercive Control* (2007) was written by:
(A) Michael Johnson  (B) Michael Kimmel  (C) Michael Kaufman  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) None of these^^ — None of these — Evan Stark.

17. The distinction between "intimate terrorism" and "situational couple violence" was drawn by:
(A) Michael Johnson  (B) Michael Kaufman  (C) Michael Kimmel  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Michael Johnson^^ — Michael Johnson.

18. Lori Heise's ecological model (1998) has four levels. Which is NOT one of them?
(A) Global  (B) Relationship  (C) Community  (D) Individual
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Global^^ — Individual, relationship, community and society.

19. "Structural violence" (1969) was defined by:
(A) R. W. Connell  (B) Lori Heise  (C) Johan Galtung  (D) Liz Kelly
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Johan Galtung^^ — Johan Galtung, who added "cultural violence" in 1990.

20. Kaufman's "triad of men's violence" (1987) includes violence against women, against other men and against:
(A) Children  (B) Property  (C) The State  (D) Themselves
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Themselves^^ — Themselves.

21. "Aggrieved entitlement" is a term of:
(A) Michael Kaufman  (B) Michael Kimmel  (C) R. W. Connell  (D) Evan Stark
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Michael Kimmel^^ — Michael Kimmel.

22. The White Ribbon Campaign of men against violence began in 1991 in:
(A) Britain  (B) Pakistan  (C) Canada  (D) Australia
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Canada^^ — Canada.

23. UN Women's HeForShe campaign was launched in:
(A) 2010  (B) 2014  (C) 2017  (D) 2021
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 2014^^ — 2014.

24. The share of ever-married women in Pakistan who experienced physical violence since age 15 (PDHS 2017–18) was:
(A) 18%  (B) 28%  (C) 34%  (D) 56%
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 28%^^ — 28% (34% spousal violence of any kind; 56% never sought help).

25. *Siyahkari* is the term for honour killing in:
(A) Balochi  (B) Sindhi  (C) Pashto  (D) Punjabi
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Balochi^^ — Balochi (*karo-kari* Sindhi, *tor tora* Pashto, *kala kali* Punjabi).

26. Exchange marriage between two families is called:
(A) *Vani*  (B) *Watta satta*  (C) *Swara*  (D) *Haq bakhshish*
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) *Watta satta*^^ — *Watta satta*.

27. The Qisas and Diyat Ordinance (1990) allowed victims' heirs to:
(A) Appeal to the FSC  (B) Demand the death penalty only  (C) Forgive the killer  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Forgive the killer^^ — Forgive the killer — the loophole later restricted in 2016.

28. The Acid Control and Acid Crime Prevention Act 2011 added which sections to the Penal Code?
(A) 310A and 310B  (B) 336A and 336B  (C) 498A and 498B  (D) 509 and 509A
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 336A and 336B^^ — Sections 336A and 336B.

29. Section 310A PPC punishes:
(A) Forced marriage  (B) Denial of inheritance  (C) Marriage to the Qur'an  (D) Giving a woman in *vani* or *swara*
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Giving a woman in *vani* or *swara*^^ — *Vani*/*swara* (498A inheritance, 498B forced marriage, 498C marriage to the Qur'an).

30. The first provincial domestic-violence law in Pakistan was passed in 2013 by:
(A) Punjab  (B) Balochistan  (C) Sindh  (D) Khyber Pakhtunkhwa
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Sindh^^ — Sindh (Balochistan 2014, Punjab 2016, KP 2021, Islamabad 2025).

31. The Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act received assent on:
(A) 1 December 2021  (B) 24 February 2016  (C) 9 October 2012  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) 1 December 2021^^ — 1 December 2021.

32. The Punjab Protection of Women against Violence Act 2016 requires the Family Court to decide complaints within:
(A) 30 days  (B) 60 days  (C) 90 days  (D) 6 months
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 90 days^^ — 90 days.

33. Under the Punjab Act 2016, a protection order may require the offender to wear:
(A) A badge  (B) A uniform  (C) A GPS bracelet  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) A GPS bracelet^^ — A GPS ankle or wrist bracelet in cases of grave violence.

34. The Punjab Protection of Women against Violence Act 2016 created:
(A) District Women Protection Committees  (B) Women Protection Officers  (C) Both A and B  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Both A and B^^ — Both.

35. The first women's police stations in Pakistan opened in:
(A) 1988  (B) 1994  (C) 2002  (D) 2017
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 1994^^ — 1994.

36. Mukhtaran Mai's memoir is titled:
(A) *I Am Malala*  (B) *In the Name of Honor*  (C) *Saving Face*  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) *In the Name of Honor*^^ — *In the Name of Honor* (2006).

37. Malala Yousafzai's BBC Urdu diary (2009) was written under the name:
(A) Zainab  (B) Saba Qaiser  (C) Gul Makai  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Gul Makai^^ — "Gul Makai".

38. Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy's Oscar-winning *Saving Face* (2012) is about:
(A) Acid attacks  (B) Honour killing  (C) Child marriage  (D) Girls' education
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Acid attacks^^ — Acid attacks; co-directed with Daniel Junge.
